 61CU c  2004Iz01: E({+40}Ca)=96 MeV beam provided by LNL Tandem accelerator,   
 61CU2c  bombarding a {+24}Mg target. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g(|q)(DCO),   
 61CU3c  |g|g(lin pol) with the EUROBALL Ge-detector array consisting of 26     
 61CU4c  Clover detectors and 15 Cluster detectors. Evaporated charged          
 61CU5c  particles were detected in the 40-element silicon |DE-E array ISIS.    
 61CU c  1999Vi07, 1999Vi12: E=65 MeV. Measured E|g, |g|g, I|g,                 
 61CU2c  and |g|g(|q)(DCO) using the AYEBALL array with TESSA type detectors,   
 61CU3c  eight EUROGAM detectors and one GAMMASPHERE detector.                  
 61CU cG $DCO=[(I(158|') gated at I(79|',101|',134|'))/( I(79|',101|',134|')    
 61CU2cG gated at I(158|'))]|*|e, where I is the number of counts in a peak     
 61CU3cG and |e is an efficiency multiplication factor (1999Vi12 and 1999Vi07). 
 61CU cG $R{-DCO}=I(|g{-1} at 156|'; gated with |g{-2} at 77|',103|')/I(|g{-1}  
 61CU2cG at 77|',103|'; gated with |g{-2} at 156|' ), CLOVER detectors at 77|'  
 61CU3cG and 103|' are equivalent as far as DCO ratios are concerned. Known     
 61CU4cG stretched E2 transitions were used for gating, such the R{-DCO}=1.0    
 61CU5cG is expected for stretched quadrupole transitions and R{-DCO}|?0.6 for  
 61CU6cG stretched dipoles, |DJ=0 transitions have values                       
 61CU7cG similar to stretched quadrupole transitions (2004Iz01).                
 61CU cG $POL=[aN(perpendicular)-N(parallel)]/[aN(perpendicular)+N(parallel)],  
 61CU2cG where a(E|g)=normalization function determined from the {+152}Eu source
 61CU3cG calibration. POL takes positive values for pure stretched electrical   
 61CU4cG radiation and negative values for pure stretched magnetic radiation    
 61CU5cG (2004Iz01).                                                            
